1. Virtual Environment
The 'env' folder is what you created with 'python -m venv env'.
This is crucial: NEVER commit the virtual environment.
env/
venv/
*.pyc
pycache/

2. Dependencies
Dependencies are installed via pip. We commit the requirements.txt, not the installed files.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

3. Django-Specific Files
Database files, logs, and sensitive data (if not using environment variables)
*.sqlite3
db.sqlite3
/media/
/static_collected/
.DS_Store

4. Environment Variables (Sensitive Data)
CRITICAL: Always ignore environment variable files that contain secrets (like DB passwords, API keys, etc.)
.env
.local.env
